From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:49:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: ppp: retain native association and accounting lifetime

Expose an opaque reference to the actual generic PPP device and channel,
with a copied native configuration/path snapshot, generation validation,
and full-width hardware-only accounting. Report committed configuration
and association changes outside the native spinlocks. Before protocol
fields disappear, permanently close that channel identity and notify
consumers so execution can be withdrawn while its old accounting survives.
No protocol socket reference, native consumer list or hardware policy is
introduced. Preserve the target's existing PPPoE GRO/GSO backport.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---

